rt: captured pre-restart boot_id (83a0a80f...), issued a non-blocking systemctl reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed a new boot_id (df4b7e15...) and fresh uptime, then re-verified crond is active and the cron.allow restriction (root/opsadmin allowed, unlisted user denied) still holds post-restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected baseline: OS (CentOS Stream 10), crond active, no /etc/cron.allow, empty /etc/cron.deny, opsadmin user absent\",\"Created opsadmin user via useradd\",\"Wrote /etc/cron.allow containing root and opsadmin (root:root, 644 perms), removed /etc/cron.deny, restarted crond\",\"Verified root and opsadmin can install/list/remove crontabs\",\"Created a throwaway unprivileged test user and confirmed crontab access is denied ('not allowed to use this program'), then cleaned it up\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and crond/cron.allow health baseline\",\"Issued non-blocking systemctl reboot on node1; acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until reachable again; confirmed changed boot_id and fresh uptime, proving an actual restart\",\"Re-verified crond active, cron.allow contents persisted, and functional allow/deny behavior (root/opsadmin allowed, new unlisted test user denied) post-restart; cleaned up second test user\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Only root and opsadmin can schedule cron jobs (configuration)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b5939a3063cf4df8\",\"cmd-38c9953d32564e6f\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline showed no /etc/cron.allow; opsadmin created and /etc/cron.allow written with root and opsadmin, cron.deny removed, crond restarted active.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Functional proof: root and opsadmin can schedule; other users cannot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-892242aeb7b0497b\",\"cmd-55fa74df4c5e4564\"],\"summary\":\"root and opsadmin successfully installed/listed crontabs; a test unprivileged user was denied with 'not allowed to use this program (crontab)', then removed.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline for node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-bdc0008273e846f2\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 83a0a80f-773c-4f3e-9137-1e7aa887b07a, crond active, cron.allow contents (root, opsadmin), cron.deny absent.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1bde5a33c68c4722\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot issued via backgrounded nohup; command acknowledged and connection subsequently dropped (stream closed), confirming reboot proceeded.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Proof of changed boot identity after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1504086a640645f7\",\"cmd-349c8aae6d984139\",\"cmd-586bb2b36a0f47b6\"],\"summary\":\"Node unreachable during reboot (timeout, connection reset), then reachable again with new boot_id df4b7e15-ff02-42de-a66b-18b9a459b1d9 and fresh uptime, differing from the pre-restart boot_id.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of cron service, config, and access control\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b0ce236c29424495\"],\"summary\":\"crond active post-restart, /etc/cron.allow persisted with root/opsadmin, cron.deny still absent, root and opsadmin successfully scheduled/removed crontabs, and a newly created unlisted test user was denied crontab access, matching pre-restart behavior.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1, cron scheduling is now restricted to root and opsadmin via /etc/cron.allow (with /etc/cron.deny removed so cron.allow is authoritative). Created the opsadmin user, verified root and opsadmin can install/list crontabs while a test unprivileged user is rejected by crontab with \"not allowed to use this program\". Performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured pre-restart boot_id (83a0a80f...), issued a non-blocking systemctl reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed a new boot_id (df4b7e15...) and fresh uptime, then re-verified crond is active and the cron.allow restriction (root/opsadmin allowed, unlisted user denied) still holds post-restart.","actions_performed":["Inspected baseline: OS (CentOS Stream 10), crond active, no /etc/cron.allow, empty /etc/cron.deny, opsadmin user absent","Created opsadmin user via useradd","Wrote /etc/cron.allow containing root and opsadmin (root:root, 644 perms), removed /etc/cron.deny, restarted crond","Verified root and opsadmin can install/list/remove crontabs","Created a throwaway unprivileged test user and confirmed crontab access is denied ('not allowed to use this program'), then cleaned it up","Captured pre-restart boot_id and crond/cron.allow health baseline","Issued non-blocking systemctl reboot on node1; acknowledgement returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until reachable again; confirmed changed boot_id and fresh uptime, proving an actual restart","Re-verified crond active, cron.allow contents persisted, and functional allow/deny behavior (root/opsadmin allowed, new unlisted test user denied) post-restart; cleaned up second test user"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Only root and opsadmin can schedule cron jobs (configuration)","command_ids":["cmd-b5939a3063cf4df8","cmd-38c9953d32564e6f"],"summary":"Baseline showed no /etc/cron.allow; opsadmin created and /etc/cron.allow written with root and opsadmin, cron.deny removed, crond restarted active."},{"requirement":"Functional proof: root and opsadmin can schedule; other users cannot","command_ids":["cmd-892242aeb7b0497b","cmd-55fa74df4c5e4564"],"summary":"root and opsadmin successfully installed/listed crontabs; a test unprivileged user was denied with 'not allowed to use this program (crontab)', then removed."},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline for node1","command_ids":["cmd-bdc0008273e846f2"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 83a0a80f-773c-4f3e-9137-1e7aa887b07a, crond active, cron.allow contents (root, opsadmin), cron.deny absent."},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-1bde5a33c68c4722"],"summary":"systemctl reboot issued via backgrounded nohup; command acknowledged and connection subsequently dropped (stream closed), confirming reboot proceeded."},{"requirement":"Proof of changed boot identity after restart","command_ids":["cmd-1504086a640645f7","cmd-349c8aae6d984139","cmd-586bb2b36a0f47b6"],"summary":"Node unreachable during reboot (timeout, connection reset), then reachable again with new boot_id df4b7e15-ff02-42de-a66b-18b9a459b1d9 and fresh uptime, differing from the pre-restart boot_id."},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of cron service, config, and access control","command_ids":["cmd-b0ce236c29424495"],"summary":"crond active post-restart, /etc/cron.allow persisted with root/opsadmin, cron.deny still absent, root and opsadmin successfully scheduled/removed crontabs, and a newly created unlisted test user was denied crontab access, matching pre-restart behavior."}]},"ttft_ms":3355,"type":"result","duration_ms":81046,"uuid":"10649305-65cb-4da9-976d-fc4d2abdff0e","ttft_stream_ms":1411,"time_to_request_ms":74,"first_content_frame_ms":1412,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
